{title: 559 - Now Thank We All Our God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #559 • NUN DANKET • 6.7.6.7.6.6.6.6}
{lyricist: Martin Rinkart}
{composer: Johann Cruger}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 559}
{meta: tune NUN DANKET}
{meta: meter 6.7.6.7.6.6.6.6}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Now thank we [Bb/D]all our God
[Eb]With heart and [Ab]hands and voices,
[Eb]Who wondrous things hath done,
[Eb]In whom His world rejoices;
[Fm]Who, from our [Gm]mothers’ arms
[Bb]Hath blessed us [Eb]onour way
[Bb]With countless gifts of love,
[Eb]And still is ours today.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]O may this [Bb/D]bounteous God
[Eb]through all our [Ab]life be near us,
[Eb]with ever joyful hearts
[Eb]and blessed peace to cheer us;
[Fm]and keep us [Gm]still in grace,
[Bb]and guide us [Eb]when perplexed;
[Bb]and free us from all ills,
[Eb]in this world and the next.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]All praise and [Bb/D]thanks to God
[Eb]the Father [Ab]now be given;
[Eb]the Son, and Him who reigns
[Eb]with them in highest heaven;
[Fm]the one eternal [Gm]God,
[Bb]whom earth and heaven [Eb]adore;
[Bb]for thus it was, is now,
[Eb]and shall be evermore.
{end_of_verse}
